== Related Work

Visual search in fashion e-commerce is a well-established field, yet a significant gap remains in accessible implementation for small-to-medium enterprises (SMEs). Current solutions typically fall into two extremes: proprietary "black-box" SaaS platforms that require expensive subscriptions, or purely academic research that focuses on algorithmic novelty while neglecting the engineering challenges of production integration.

This project addresses this gap by providing a transparent, end-to-end engineering blueprint for integrating visual intelligence into a modern web stack. Unlike purely theoretical studies, this research focuses on the *operationalization* of state-of-the-art models like *Fashion-CLIP* within a polyglot architecture, utilizing commodity hardware and open-source tools to democratize advanced semantic search.

A more comprehensive review of the theoretical background, existing commercial systems, and the technical positioning of this project is provided in @chap1.
